{"title":"2006 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a prime number and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be an integer with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f33cc23b9f4db7b967f7234c222d7c27402ca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;s&lt;p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that there exist integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c94d4782aebf61164830f2c330328632f5d437bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;m&lt;n&lt;p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"117\" height=\"16\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/9581af3898d23280cf0665fa293ea87429cd0c9d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\lbrace\\frac{sm}{p}\\right\\rbrace&lt;\\left\\lbrace\\frac{sn}{p}\\right\\rbrace&lt;\\frac{s}{p}\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"43\" />\nif and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is not a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/0/ab0727c08c4aaa6fa119bd3fafe17851e431fd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Note: For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> a real number, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denote the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/3/05310a9500217411a245f7bf4cdd8674d15f0bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lbrace x\\rbrace=x-\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" /> denote the fractional part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For a given positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> find, in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> for which there is a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f2789508227865dfc89fd46e18ae9b25bff34257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> distinct positive integers that has sum greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> but every subset of size <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has sum at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aaaf0b4d3eb080111baaa27f0fbe68d2057df81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For integral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/7/da754a6cd2010ce63ffe4d86138569b09678c799.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> be the greatest prime divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. By convention, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/6/216633119788123cf42efe0ecac4931d5fe35ab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(\\pm1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/5582fd35086371accc57ed8c64ff8e483cc8d970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(0)=\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />. Find all polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> with integer coefficients such that the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221ed3f7e4d1b98f43545053f779f88fef71898a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lbrace p(f(n^2))-2n\\rbrace_{n\\ge0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" /> is bounded above. (In particular, this requires <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f567d2f696f2e698a52916efe8ec20a2afa8ea70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n^2)\\neq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/9013bb191380c197d4fbea9ef176b90631bde0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which there exists an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e4194d33d81c3dd5ac49c773335504c4a7a0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and positive rationals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56cf1a6c9e2b306fd81ecb7f1076e119d6ab3b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\ldots a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"11\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/a/0ca01eadd2b616e9d5ede870d57f53525c140b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+\\ldots+a_k=a_1\\cdot a_2\\cdots a_k=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"291\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A mathematical frog jumps along the number line. The frog starts at 1, and jumps according to the following rule: if the frog is at integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, then it can jump either to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> or to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/4948eb6c7b0070d6c560380e4b8aa8324dc0932a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2^{m_n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fa7675310996f37589003b32e49e94315a7b19e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m_n}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is the largest power of 2 that is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/291d1481161e5339e53d6caea42174d1a0d71898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> is a positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is a nonnegative integer, then the minimum number of jumps needed to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f929a3f1a6d796c6fb013cf74577690331c1f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^ik$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> is greater than the minimum number of jumps needed to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4b92d67419c77c7a9bab9103274256eb1ba428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^i$\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a quadrilateral, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be points on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/2799ac7a517b8c68a7f6a23a9d10d82dad5357d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE/ED=BF/FC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />.  Ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> meets rays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Prove that the circumcircles of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f47dbc8698fb952c998a24ac10289ba27dc8b017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SAE$\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/7/fa70cbcea4b7783ea6de25ffaf46762b074416fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SBF$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54f1d51048f287587db9a2595f8ab56f34691077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TCF$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/275a794bbac31542090ef480457049b21351c098.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TDE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> pass through a common point.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO\" title=\"2006 USAMO\">2006 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO\" title=\"2005 USAMO\">2005 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO\" title=\"2007 USAMO\">2007 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018052845\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 317/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1255/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 64/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10010/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.343      1 -total\n 60.25%    8.039      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 37.40%    4.990      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2501:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018052845 and revision id 249622. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}